// Seven equal bars, 3:5 (the designer's 540 by 324 image).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Pomosexual flag"
  designer "pride-color-schemes (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20181217214044/https://pride-color-schemes.tumblr.com/post/146935072870/pomo"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20181219000748/https://66.media.tumblr.com/1b0af1ec6788d21f85fa0a98573323bf/tumblr_inline_obdm3ovUpE1re2bou_540.png"
  note "Designer's own post: 'Pomo-' on the Tumblr blog pride-color-schemes, dated 5 July 2016 and posted by its account kiloueka (Wayback Machine, 17 December 2018). It defines pomo- as an orientation where one denies or doesn't fit any labels for a kind of attraction, or 'not straight' without a more precise label. It shows two earlier designs by @pastelmemer and @lgbtrainbowdolls, then 'Pomosexual: a flag with seven stripes. from top to bottom they are: pink, light pink, white, purple, white, light pink, pink', 'Designed by : Me'. It gives no color meanings for this design. The post may have been edited after its date, so no date is given here."
  note "The proportion, equal stripes and colors are read from the post's image, 540 by 324 pixels (3:5) with stripes of about 46: #ffaec9, #ffc6de, #ffffff, #e8cdff, #ffffff, #ffc6de and #ffaec9. The post calls the middle stripe purple; it is a pale lavender."
}
palette {
  pink "#ffaec9"
  light-pink "#ffc6de"
  white "#ffffff"
  lavender "#e8cdff"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars pink light-pink white lavender white light-pink pink
